## 2. Fonts and Typography Assets
All font files (.woff2, .ttf) hosted in this repository are subsetted derivatives or original distributions of open-source / open-data fonts. Copyrights belong to their respective authors:

### A. SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-1.1)
The following fonts and their subsets are released under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1:
- **ChillKai (寒蝉正楷體)** & **ChillHuoFangSong (寒蟬活仿宋)** - Copyright (c) Warren2060
- **Zhuque Fangsong (朱雀仿宋)** - Copyright (c) TrionesType
- **Iansui (芫荽體)** - Copyright (c) 2021 ButTaiwan
- **Instrument Sans (Latin Subset)** - Copyright (c) 2022 Rodrigo Fuenzalida, Jordan Bell

*(See Appendix A below for the full SIL OFL 1.1 text)*

### B. ARPHIC PUBLIC LICENSE (ARPHICPL)
The following fonts and their subsets are released under the ARPHIC Public License:
- **AR PL UKai (文鼎中楷)** (TW / CN) - Copyright (C) 1999 Arphic Technology Co., Ltd. / Debian / Ubuntu CJK-Unifonts Community
- **AR PL UMing (文鼎細上海宋)** (TW / CN) - Copyright (C) 1999 Arphic Technology Co., Ltd. / Debian / Ubuntu CJK-Unifonts Community

*(See Appendix B below or `ukai-tw/license/` for the full ARPHICPL text)*

### C. Open Government Data License (OGDL 1.0)
The following fonts and their subsets are derived from Chinese Standard Interchange Code (CNS 11643):
- **TW-Kai & TW-Sung (全字庫正楷體 / 全字庫正宋體 Ext-B & 標點符號子集)**
  Released by the Ministry of Digital Affairs / National Development Council (Taiwan) under Open Government Data License (OGDL-Taiwan-1.0).

### D. Custom Open / Free for Commercial Use
- **Huiwen Fangsong (匯文仿宋)**
  Recreated by Terry Wang (特里王) based on 59-4 type. Free for commercial and non-commercial use, prohibited from being sold or monetized by third parties as declared by the original creator.

